<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Abbas II of Persia</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Abbas II</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Abbas II of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/persia">Persia</a> was a Safavid shah who ruled from 1642 to 1666. His reign was relatively stable and included the recovery of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kandahar">Kandahar</a> from the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mughal-empire">Mughals</a>, and he took a personal interest in government. In the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/safavid-empire">Safavid Empire</a>'s profile he appears as one of the later shahs whose rule preceded the dynasty's more pronounced decline.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/abbas-ii-of-persia.jpg" alt="Abbas II of Persia" width="259" height="420" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Circa 1647 · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Abbas_II_of_Persia,_Palace_of_Chehel_Sotoun._Painted_circa_1647.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
